You are debugging a production issue where a mission-critical gateway service experiences an `OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` after running for several days. A developer wrote the following custom cache to retain session contexts while automatically allowing idle user objects to be reclaimed under memory pressure:

java
public class SessionRegistry {
    private final Map<UserSession, SessionContext> cache =
            Collections.synchronizedMap(new WeakHashMap<>());

    public void registerSession(UserSession session) {
        cache.computeIfAbsent(session, s -> new SessionContext(s, System.currentTimeMillis()));
    }

    public SessionContext getContext(UserSession session) {
        return cache.get(session);
    }
}

class SessionContext {
    private final UserSession session;
    private final long createdAt;

    public SessionContext(UserSession session, long createdAt) {
        this.session = session;
        this.createdAt = createdAt;
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an enterprise inventory system running on Spring Boot and Hibernate generates severe database lock contention and performance degradation. An engineer refactored a service method that updates the lines of an `Order` aggregate:

java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired private OrderRepository orderRepo;

    @Transactional
    public void updateOrderLines(Long orderId, Set<OrderLine> newLines) {
        Order order = orderRepo.findById(orderId).orElseThrow();
        order.setOrderLines(new HashSet<>(newLines));
        orderRepo.save(order);
    }
}


During high concurrency, SQL tracing reveals that Hibernate executes an unexpected `DELETE` query against all existing rows in the child table followed by batch `INSERT` statements for every item in `newLines`, rather than differential `UPDATE`, `INSERT`, and `DELETE` statements.

You are debugging a production issue where a low-latency financial order matcher suffers from severe throughput collapse and elevated p99 latencies across multiple CPU cores. Profiling shows high CPI (Cycles Per Instruction) and extreme cache line invalidations (`L1-dcache-load-misses`) in the following custom multi-threaded ring buffer:

java
public class SequencedRingBuffer<T> {
    private final Object[] entries;
    private final int mask;

    // Head written by single consumer; Tail written by producers
    private volatile long head = 0L;
    private volatile long tail = 0L;

    public SequencedRingBuffer(int capacity) {
        this.entries = new Object[capacity];
        this.mask = capacity - 1;
    }

    public void produce(T item) { /* updates tail via CAS */ }
    public T consume() { /* updates head via CAS */ }
}
